# Analyst Notes

Registry modifications are frequently used by threat actors to establish persistence, bypass security controls, or alter operating system behavior. Although registry changes occur regularly during legitimate software installation and system administration, modifications affecting persistence locations or security-related keys should always receive additional scrutiny.

This detection becomes significantly more valuable when correlated with PowerShell execution, Command Prompt activity, Scheduled Task creation, Service creation, and Privileged Logon events, allowing analysts to reconstruct the complete attack sequence.
